## Notes per locale

- `ar` — Arabic (RTL, CLDR requires all six plural quantities: zero, one, two, few, many, other)
- `de` — German (informal/direct UI register)
- `el` — Greek (standard modern Greek UI terminology)
- `es` — Spanish (standard direct second-person "tú")
- `fr` — French (standard polite UI register "vous")
- `hi` — Hindi
- `in` — Indonesian (Android's legacy code `in`, never write `id` in CSV)
- `it` — Italian
- `ja` — Japanese (standard polite Japanese UI conventions)
- `ko` — Korean (standard polite Korean UI conventions)
- `pl` — Polish (standard direct UI register)
- `pt-BR` — Brazilian Portuguese (uses "você", "celular", "tela")
- `ro` — Romanian
- `ru` — Russian (inflects nouns by case and plural forms)
- `tr` — Turkish
- `uk` — Ukrainian
- `vi` — Vietnamese (uses pronoun "bạn", "cài đặt" for install, "gỡ cài đặt" for uninstall)
- `zh` — Simplified Chinese (简体中文: uses "安装", "设置", "卸载", "正在卸载…")
